Author: b <a@b>
Date:   Tue Sep 29 11:00:00 2026 -0700

    REFACTOR-0009: pull the status rules out of printStatus

    TEST-0009 listed the status command's tests but couldn't write any of
    them: printStatus() reads the day from the clock and prints its answer
    instead of returning it.

    Extracts messageFor(offeringId, today): the same rules, but it is
    handed the day instead of reading the clock, and it returns the message
    instead of printing it. printStatus() is left doing only the two things
    a test still can't control: asking the clock for today, and printing.

    Fills in TEST-0009's tests against messageFor, each picking the day it
    needs.

